# Emet-Selch, Unsundered (2/4 vigilance): "Whenever Emet-Selch enters or attacks, draw a card, then discard a card." Turn 1 Bot1 casts every other card of its hand, so its hand is empty when
# Emet-Selch enters: the card it draws (a Memnite) is the only one it can discard, which discarding first could not do. On turn 3 it draws a Savannah Lions, attacks (the Island
# the trigger draws joins it in hand) and discards the older Lions: the discard is chosen among both. Vigilance leaves it untapped; Bot2 takes 2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Black Lotus
Emet-Selch, Unsundered
Memnite
Savannah Lions
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Emet-Selch, Unsundered.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Memnite)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 1
? Bot1.Graveyard = Memnite
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Emet-Selch, Unsundered)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Savannah Lions)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Savannah Lions; Memnite
Bot1.Hand = Island
Bot1.Battlefield.Emet-Selch, Unsundered.Tapped = false
Bot2.Life = 18
